---
import Arrow from '../components/common/Arrow.astro';
import HomeGlass from '../components/common/HomeGlass.astro';
import '../styles/brand-center.css';
const colors = [
 {name:'Jet Black',hex:'#252525',use:'The foundation. Dark chapters, display type, and contrast.'},
 {name:'Studio White',hex:'#FFFFFF',use:'The breathing room. Light chapters and reversed lettering.'},
 {name:'Sky Blue',hex:'#93E9F9',use:'The signature interaction. Title highlights and cool glass.'},
 {name:'Soft Pink',hex:'#FDBFBF',use:'The human touch. Warm accents and inviting actions.'},
 {name:'Spotlight Yellow',hex:'#EFDA4A',use:'The spark. A clear, energetic point of attention.'},
 {name:'Fresh Mint',hex:'#7CF5B5',use:'The invitation. Fresh accents and a friendly next step.'},
];
const chapters = ['Essence','Color','Type','Material','Motion','Voice','Assets'];
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
 <head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8" /><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
  <meta name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow, noarchive" />
  <meta name="description" content="The colors, typography, glass, motion, and personality behind Jet Sullivan and Jet × Ben." />
  <link rel="icon" type="image/png" href="/brand-center-favicon.png" /><title>Jet Sullivan</title>
 </head>
 <body>
  <a class="skip-link" href="#essence">Skip to the guide</a>
  <section class="brand-hero scene" aria-labelledby="brand-title">
   <HomeGlass />
   <header class="brand-header wrap"><a href="/">JET SULLIVAN <span>↗</span></a><span>BRAND CENTER / FIELD GUIDE</span></header>
   <div class="wrap hero-content">
    <p class="eyebrow">The look. The feeling. The details.</p>
    <h1 id="brand-title" aria-label="Jet Sullivan"><span class="hero-name-layer hero-name-base" aria-hidden="true">{Array.from('JET SULLIVAN').map((letter,index)=><span class="hero-letter" data-letter-index={index}>{letter === ' ' ? '\u00a0' : letter}</span>)}</span></h1>
    <div class="hero-bottom"><div><p class="hero-statement">Bold by nature.<br />Playful in the details.</p><p>A visual language for an actor, a filmmaker, and the stories worth sharing.</p></div><p class="hero-note">Black & white at rest.<br />A little blue when you get close.<span>Move across the letters ↗</span></p></div>
   </div>
  </section>
  <nav class="chapter-nav" aria-label="Brand guide chapters"><div class="wrap">{chapters.map((chapter,index)=><a href={`#${chapter.toLowerCase()}`}><small>0{index+1}</small>{chapter}</a>)}</div></nav>
  <main>
   <section id="essence" class="chapter scene"><HomeGlass tone="pink" variant="about" /><div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">01 / The essence</p><h2>Clean structure.<br />Real personality.</h2><p>Big, confident type gives the work a stage. Black and white hold it together. Color, glass, and a little physical play make it feel unmistakably human.</p></div>
    <div class="reference-grid">
     <a class="reference" href="/"><div class="reference-art mini-home" aria-hidden="true"><strong>JET SULLIVAN</strong><div class="mini-tabs"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></div></div><span class="eyebrow">The individual</span><h3>Jet Sullivan <Arrow /></h3><p>A striking name, a personal introduction, and four colorful paths into the work.</p></a>
     <a class="reference" href="https://benstapleton.jetsullivan.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><div class="reference-art mini-team" aria-hidden="true"><strong>JET × BEN</strong><div class="mini-tabs"><i></i><i></i><i></i></div></div><span class="eyebrow">The collaboration</span><h3>Jet × Ben <Arrow /></h3><p>The same diagonal divide and confident scale, with editorial chapters built around shared stories.</p><span class="sr-only">Opens in a new tab</span></a>
     <a class="reference" href="/socials/"><div class="reference-art mini-social" aria-hidden="true"><strong>SOCIALS</strong><div class="mini-tabs"><i></i><i></i><i></i></div></div><span class="eyebrow">The connection</span><h3>Socials <Arrow /></h3><p>The same glass and responsive lettering, with platform colors glowing through a darker surface.</p></a>
    </div>
    <p class="margin-note">Three expressions of one system. The studies above simplify the live pages; open each to explore the full experience.</p>
   </div></section>
   <section id="color" class="chapter dark scene"><HomeGlass tone="blue" variant="media" /><div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">02 / Color</p><h2>Let contrast lead.<br /><span class="blue-ink">Let color speak.</span></h2><p>Build the page in Jet Black and Studio White. Give an action or a section its own accent. Keep the name monochrome until interaction brings in Sky Blue.</p></div>
    <div class="palette">{colors.map(color=><button class="swatch" data-copy-color={color.hex} aria-label={`Copy ${color.name}, ${color.hex}`}><span class="color-chip" style={`background:${color.hex}`} aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="swatch-name">{color.name}</span><span class="hex">{color.hex} <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></span><span class="color-use">{color.use}</span></button>)}</div>
    <p class="margin-note">Click a swatch to copy its hex. Use dark text on pastel fills; reserve pale text for dark surfaces.</p>
    <aside class="rule-note"><strong>The Socials exception.</strong><p>Instagram’s multicolor glow, TikTok’s cyan and pink, and the other platforms’ own colors identify their destinations. They belong on those links; the core identity stays within the six colors above.</p></aside>
   </div></section>
   <section id="type" class="chapter scene"><HomeGlass tone="mint" variant="gear" /><div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">03 / Typography & composition</p><h2>Say it big.<br />Give it space.</h2></div>
    <div class="type-grid"><div class="type-specimen"><span class="eyebrow">Arial Black / Display</span><p class="big-type">Stories<br />worth<br /><span>sharing.</span></p><p class="type-caption">Heavy weight. Tight tracking. Solid letterforms.</p></div><div class="type-details"><div><span class="eyebrow">Myriad Pro / Body</span><p class="body-specimen">Real people. Meaningful moments. A thoughtful eye for the details that make a story yours.</p><p>Use Myriad Pro when available, with Myriad and Arial as fallbacks. Keep body copy open and easy to read.</p></div><dl><div><dt>Display</dt><dd>Arial Black, Arial, sans-serif · 900 weight</dd></div><div><dt>Body</dt><dd>16–18px · generous line spacing</dd></div><div><dt>Eyebrows</dt><dd>Small, bold capitals · spaced lettering</dd></div><div><dt>Page rhythm</dt><dd>Wide gutters · short paragraphs · one clear next step</dd></div></dl></div></div>
    <div class="rules-row"><article><h3>The signature divide.</h3><p>A diagonal moves from black into white. Letter color follows the surface beneath it so the title reads as one continuous statement.</p></article><article><h3>Space does the framing.</h3><p>Alternate light and dark chapters. Let a small eyebrow introduce a large headline, then a short thought and a clear action.</p></article><article><h3>Room on every screen.</h3><p>Stack columns on mobile, scale titles to fit, and keep moving letters clear of the edges. Preserve comfortable touch targets.</p></article></div>
   </div></section>
   <section id="material" class="chapter dark scene"><HomeGlass tone="pink" variant="contact" /><div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">04 / Shape & surface</p><h2>Soft glass.<br />A little glow.</h2><p>Circles and rounded squares form the background. A quiet tint, a thin light edge, and a soft inner highlight give them depth. Keep their centers clear of important copy.</p></div>
    <div class="material-grid"><div class="material-study" aria-label="A tinted glass circle and rounded square"><span class="study-square" data-home-motion="far"></span><span class="study-circle" data-home-motion="deep"></span><span class="study-label">Simple forms. Layered light.</span></div><div class="material-copy"><h3>Light follows your hand.</h3><p>Buttons carry more color than the background. Their rounded shape, glassy shine, and soft glow make the next step easy to find.</p><div class="button-samples"><a class="glass-button" style="--accent:#93e9f9" href="/socials/">Socials <Arrow /></a><a class="glass-button" style="--accent:#fdbfbf" href="/acting/">Acting <Arrow /></a><a class="glass-button" style="--accent:#efda4a" href="/film/">Film <Arrow /></a><a class="glass-button" style="--accent:#7cf5b5" href="/video/">Video <Arrow /></a></div><p class="margin-note">Live links, with a pointer-following shine. Pill actions and rounded cards share the same material.</p></div></div>
   </div></section>
   <section id="motion" class="chapter scene"><HomeGlass variant="about" /><div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">05 / Motion</p><h2>It has weight.<br />It finds its way home.</h2><p>Motion is a response to the person exploring. The title above uses the homepage’s actual spring behavior, and the glass throughout this guide uses its weighted parallax.</p></div>
    <div class="rules-row numbered"><article><span>01</span><h3>Touch, then return.</h3><p>Letters gently repel the cursor, light up blue, and settle back into their original place. The word stays anchored and readable.</p></article><article><span>02</span><h3>Depth as you move.</h3><p>Cursor movement shifts the scene subtly. Glass layers travel at different depths; larger shapes feel slower and heavier.</p></article><article><span>03</span><h3>Ease into the scroll.</h3><p>Background forms follow scrolling with a soft lag, then settle. Content keeps a steady reading order and a clear visual hierarchy.</p></article></div>
    <aside class="rule-note"><strong>Keep it comfortable.</strong><p>Respect reduced-motion preferences. On small screens, use gentler movement and stacked layouts. Links stay usable by touch and keyboard, with a visible focus state.</p></aside>
   </div></section>
   <section id="voice" class="chapter dark scene"><HomeGlass tone="mint" variant="media" /><div class="wrap voice-grid"><div><p class="eyebrow">06 / Voice & imagery</p><h2>A person.<br /><span class="mint-ink">Not a pitch.</span></h2><p>Write like Jet is in the room: direct, curious, and welcoming. Short sentences carry the idea. Real portraits and real work carry the personality.</p></div><div class="voice-examples"><blockquote>“Let’s make something.”<cite>A warm, specific invitation.</cite></blockquote><blockquote>“Tools for the story.”<cite>The equipment serves the work.</cite></blockquote><blockquote>“Two filmmakers. One shared vision.”<cite>A simple idea with a human center.</cite></blockquote><p class="margin-note">Use portraits with breathing room. Let photography feel personal, and keep decorative glass behind the subject.</p></div></div></section>
   <section id="assets" class="chapter scene"><HomeGlass tone="pink" variant="gear" /><div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">07 / The essentials</p><h2>Make it feel<br />like Jet.</h2><p>Start with the real assets. Keep proportions intact, choose the crop for the space, and let the surrounding layout do the rest.</p></div>
    <div class="asset-grid"><a href="/jet-portrait-background.PNG" download><div class="asset-image"><img src="/jet-portrait-background.PNG" alt="Jet Sullivan portrait" loading="lazy" /></div><h3>Portrait PNG <Arrow /></h3><p>Original portrait · Download</p></a><a href="/jet-portrait.jpg" download><div class="asset-image"><img src="/jet-portrait.jpg" alt="Jet Sullivan web portrait" loading="lazy" /></div><h3>Web portrait <Arrow /></h3><p>JPG · Download</p></a><a href="/jet-profile.png" download><div class="asset-image profile-image"><img src="/jet-profile.png" alt="Jet Sullivan profile image" loading="lazy" /></div><h3>Profile image <Arrow /></h3><p>Square PNG · Download</p></a></div>
    <div class="closing"><p>Bold type. Quiet space. Color with purpose.<br /><strong>A little play makes it yours.</strong></p><a class="glass-button" style="--accent:#7cf5b5" href="mailto:contact@jetsullivan.com">Let’s talk <Arrow /></a></div>
   </div></section>
  </main>
  <footer class="wrap"><a href="/">Jet Sullivan</a><span>Brand Center · Direct-access resource</span><a href="#brand-title">Back to top ↑</a></footer>
  <p class="copy-status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
 </body>
</html>
<script>
 import '../scripts/brand-center';
</script>
